I take the bill in my hand.
I get up from the table.
I go back to the front counter.
That elderly man is sitting there.
I give him the paper of the bill.
I ask, "Chacha, how much is it?"
He looks at the bill.
He smiles and says, "Madam, one hundred and fifty rupees."
I take money out of my bag.
I give him one hundred and fifty rupees.
I say, "Please take this."
"The food was very good."
He is happy.
I ask, "Will I get a receipt?"
He gives me the receipt.
He says, "Thank you madam."
"Come again."
I also say thank you to him.
Now I come out of the café.
It is evening time in Mumbai.
There is a lot of crowd on the street outside.
I like this place very much.
